## Findings

### AUTH-001: JWT Signature Not Verified — `jwt.decode()` Used Instead of `jwt.verify()`

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Rule ID** | AUTH-001 |
| **Severity** | **CRITICAL** |
| **Confidence** | 99% |
| **Location** | Line 5: `const decoded = jwt.decode(token);` |

**Description:**

The middleware uses `jwt.decode(token)` which **only base64-decodes the payload without verifying the cryptographic signature**. This means any attacker can forge an arbitrary JWT with `{"role": "admin"}` in the payload using any tool (e.g., [jwt.io](https://jwt.io)), and the middleware will accept it as a valid admin token.

Per the `jsonwebtoken` library documentation:
- `jwt.decode()` — does **not** verify the signature.
- `jwt.verify(token, secret, options)` — verifies the signature, expiration, and other claims.

**Concrete exploit:**

An attacker crafts this payload with **no valid signature**:
```
eyJhbGciOiJub25lIiwidHlwIjoiSldUIn0.eyJyb2xlIjoiYWRtaW4iLCJzdWIiOiJhdHRhY2tlciJ9.
```
This decodes to `{"role": "admin", "sub": "attacker"}`. The middleware on line 6 checks `decoded.role === "admin"` — it passes, and the attacker gets full admin access.

This violates:
- **OWASP Authentication Cheat Sheet** — "Always verify the JWT signature server-side."
- **NIST SP 800-63b** — authentication tokens must be cryptographically validated.
- **RFC 8725 (JWT BCP)** §2.1 — "Applications MUST verify the signature before trusting any claim."

**Recommendation:**

Replace `jwt.decode()` with `jwt.verify()`, specifying the secret/key and restricting the allowed algorithms:

```typescript
import jwt from "jsonwebtoken";

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(" ")[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).send("No token");

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET!, {
      algorithms: ["HS256"], // explicit algorithm restriction
    });
    if ((decoded as any).role === "admin") {
      req.user = decoded;
      next();
    } else {
      res.status(403).send("Forbidden");
    }
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(401).send("Invalid token");
  }
});
```

