CLDR defines six plural categories (`zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`, `other`). Languages like Arabic use all six, Polish and Russian use `one`/`few`/`many`/`other`, and Welsh uses `zero`/`one`/`two`/`few`/`many`/`other`. The code's own comment on line 6 acknowledges this defect.

