# Framework Safety Evaluation

## Findings

### FW-001: IntersectionObserver re-created on every `page` change without cleanup
- **Rule ID:** FW-001
- **Severity:** High
- **Category:** React Rules of Hooks — Effect cleanup / dependency array
- **Location:** Lines 5–17 (`useEffect` block)
- **Evidence:**

The `useEffect` depends on `[page]`. Every time `page` increments (line 12), the effect re-runs, creating a **new** `IntersectionObserver` and calling `observer.observe(...)` again — without ever disconnecting the previous observer. After N pages, there are N live observers all watching the same sentinel, each of which will fire and trigger redundant fetches.

Additionally, inside the observer callback, `setPage(p => p + 1)` (line 12) causes `page` to change, which re-triggers the effect, which creates yet another observer — producing an unbounded cascading loop that fires multiple concurrent fetches for the same or successive pages every time the sentinel intersects.

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    // ...
    setPage(p => p + 1); // triggers effect re-run
  });
  observer.observe(document.getElementById("sentinel")!);
  // ← no return () => observer.disconnect();
}, [page]); // ← re-runs on every page change
```

- **Recommendation:**

1. **Return a cleanup function** to disconnect the observer when the effect re-runs or the component unmounts.
2. **Remove `page` from the dependency array** (use a ref for the current page value instead) so the observer is created once and stable.

```typescript
const pageRef = useRef(1);

useEffect(() => {
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    if (entries[0].isIntersecting) {
      const currentPage = pageRef.current;
      fetch(`/api/products?page=${currentPage}`)
        .then(r => r.json())
        .then(data => {
          setProducts(prev => [...prev, ...data]);
          pageRef.current += 1;
        });
    }
  });

  const sentinel = document.getElementById("sentinel");
  if (sentinel) observer.observe(sentinel);

  return () => observer.disconnect(); // cleanup
}, []); // stable dependency array
```

- **Reference:** [React docs — Synchronizing with Effects: cleanup](https://react.dev/learn/synchronizing-with-effects#step-3-add-cleanup-if-needed)

