### CYBER-001: LDAP Injection via Unsanitized User Input

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | **CRITICAL** |
| **CWE** | CWE-90 (LDAP Injection) |
| **OWASP** | A03:2021 – Injection |
| **Line** | 21 |

**Evidence:**

```java
String filter = "(&(uid=" + username + ")(userPassword=" + password + "))";
```

Both `username` and `password` are concatenated directly into the LDAP search filter string with zero sanitization or escaping. An attacker can inject arbitrary LDAP filter syntax to bypass authentication entirely.

**Exploit Scenario:**

An attacker supplies:
- `username`: `*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*`
- `password`: anything

This produces the filter:
```
(&(uid=*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*)(userPassword=anything))
```

The first clause `(&(uid=*)(uid=*))` matches every user in the directory. `results.hasMore()` on line 26 returns `true`, and authentication succeeds without valid credentials.

Even simpler — supplying `username = *` and `password = *` yields `(&(uid=*)(userPassword=*))` which matches any entry that has both attributes present.

**Remediation:**

1. **Escape special LDAP characters** in all user-supplied values before filter construction. RFC 4515 defines characters that must be escaped: `*`, `(`, `)`, `\`, `NUL`.

2. **Prefer LDAP bind authentication** instead of search-based password comparison (passwords should never appear in search filters).

3. Use a dedicated escaping utility:

```java
// Option A: Manual escaping per RFC 4515
private static String escapeLdapFilter(String input) {
    if (input == null) return "";
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
    for (char c : input.toCharArray()) {
        switch (c) {
            case '\\': sb.append("\\5c"); break;
            case '*':  sb.append("\\2a"); break;
            case '(':  sb.append("\\28"); break;
            case ')':  sb.append("\\29"); break;
            case '\0': sb.append("\\00"); break;
            default:   sb.append(c);
        }
    }
    return sb.toString();
}

// Option B (preferred): Use LDAP bind for authentication
public boolean authenticate(String username, String password) {
    String escapedUser = escapeLdapFilter(username);
    String userDn = "uid=" + escapedUser + "," + BASE_DN;

    Hashtable<String, String> env = new Hashtable<>();
    env.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
    env.put(Context.PROVIDER_URL, LDAP_URL);
    env.put(Context.SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION, "simple");
    env.put(Context.SECURITY_PRINCIPAL, userDn);
    env.put(Context.SECURITY_CREDENTIALS, password);

    try {
        DirContext ctx = new InitialDirContext(env);
        ctx.close();
        return true;
    } catch (AuthenticationException e) {
        return false;
    } catch (NamingException e) {
        return false;
    }
}
```

