2. **The password is transmitted as part of the query**, making it visible in LDAP server logs, network traces, and debug output (reinforced by `e.printStackTrace()` on line 29).
3. **Anonymous bind on line 18** (`new InitialDirContext(env)` with no `SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION` or `SECURITY_PRINCIPAL`) means the search runs without authenticating the application itself, and password comparison in the filter is entirely dependent on LDAP server ACLs exposing `userPassword`.

**Recommendation:**

Use LDAP bind authentication — the standard secure pattern. First search for the user DN, then attempt to bind as that user with their password:

```java
public boolean authenticate(String username, String password) {
    try {
        // 1. Search for user DN with a service account (or anonymous if allowed)
        Hashtable<String, String> env = new Hashtable<>();
        env.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
        env.put(Context.PROVIDER_URL, "ldaps://ldap.company.com:636");
        env.put(Context.SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION, "simple");
        env.put(Context.SECURITY_PRINCIPAL, SERVICE_ACCOUNT_DN);
        env.put(Context.SECURITY_CREDENTIALS, SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD);

        DirContext ctx = new InitialDirContext(env);

        // Sanitize username for the search filter
        String sanitizedUser = sanitizeLdapFilter(username);
        String filter = "(uid=" + sanitizedUser + ")";
        SearchControls sc = new SearchControls();
        sc.setSearchScope(SearchControls.SUBTREE_SCOPE);
        sc.setReturningAttributes(new String[]{"dn"});

        NamingEnumeration<?> results = ctx.search(BASE_DN, filter, sc);
        if (!results.hasMore()) { ctx.close(); return false; }

        String userDn = ((SearchResult) results.next()).getNameInNamespace();
        ctx.close();

        // 2. Attempt to bind as the user
        Hashtable<String, String> userEnv = new Hashtable<>();
        userEnv.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
        userEnv.put(Context.PROVIDER_URL, "ldaps://ldap.company.com:636");
        userEnv.put(Context.SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION, "simple");
        userEnv.put(Context.SECURITY_PRINCIPAL, userDn);
        userEnv.put(Context.SECURITY_CREDENTIALS, password);

        DirContext userCtx = new InitialDirContext(userEnv);
        userCtx.close();
        return true;
    } catch (AuthenticationException e) {
        return false;
    } catch (NamingException e) {
        return false;
    }
}
```

