### PERF-002: O(n²) Linear Scan for Deduplication in `deduplicateByField`

**Severity**: high
**Location**: Lines 20–28 (nested `for` loop scanning `result` array)

**Description**: For each incoming item (line 21), the function performs a linear scan of the accumulated `result` array (lines 23–27) to check for duplicates. This is O(n²) in the number of items. For a list of 10,000 items, this is ~50 million comparisons.

**Evidence**: Line 23 — `for (const existing of result)` iterates the entire result so far for every new item, using equality comparison on a dynamic field.

**Recommendation**: Use a `Set` (or `Map`) keyed on the field value for O(1) lookups:

```typescript
function deduplicateByField<T>(items: T[], field: keyof T): T[] {
  const seen = new Set<unknown>();
  const result: T[] = [];
  for (const item of items) {
    const key = item[field];
    if (!seen.has(key)) {
      seen.add(key);
      result.push(item);
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

This reduces time complexity to O(n) and also provides type safety by replacing `any[]` with a generic.

